<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3885"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Skov<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Skov<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, January 10, 2005 - 1:23 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Hi Tom <BR>Happy Birthday &#40;a little late sorry&#41; and take care in wichita! <BR> <BR>I wanted to ask if it is possible to make a thred where you can put all the posts that you consider misplaced/off topic, on the thred. <BR>I mean posts that, in som way, realy has a message, opinion or a reply to another posters thought, idea or info. <BR>The problem is that when one read a post that IS on topic but ALSO add som other ideas/info/thoughts one often wants to respond to that but then you always deleet those posts and they are gone for ever EVEN if they often contain very usefull info/thoughts. <BR>Like today, I read a post somone wrote, about that BTK was, among other thing, driven by hate to Wichita, and I REALY wanted to get in tuch with that poster, VERY IMPORTENT &#40;please help me out finding this poster???&#41; <BR>Now if ther was som kind of creative garbage-can thred that you could through all them off topic posts into, then we would be able to find all those posts that people have used time and brains to create. <BR>PLEASE! <BR> <BR>skov<!--/Text--></td></tr>
